PRIVACY POLICY FOR DAILY CROSSWORD

Last updated: June 6, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how our company 
handles information in connection with the mobile application Daily Crossword
(the "App"). By downloading or using the App, you agree to this Privacy Policy.

1. INFORMATION WE COLLECT

We do not require you to create an account, and we do not ask you for personal
information such as your name, email address, or phone number to play the App.

a) Information stored on your device
The App saves your game data — such as level progress, stars, coins, daily
streaks, achievements, statistics, and your settings — locally on your device.
This data stays on your device and is not transmitted to us.

b) Information collected automatically by third parties
If the App displays advertisements or uses analytics, our third-party partners
(for example, Google AdMob and Google Play services) may automatically collect
certain information, which may include:
  - a device advertising identifier (Advertising ID);
  - approximate, non-precise location derived from your IP address;
  - device information (such as device model, operating system version, and
    language);
  - app usage and crash diagnostics.
This information is collected directly by those partners under their own
privacy policies. We do not control and are not responsible for their practices.

2. HOW INFORMATION IS USED

Information may be used to:
  - save and restore your game progress on your device;
  - display and measure advertisements, including non-personalized or
    personalized ads where permitted;
  - understand app performance, fix crashes, and improve the App.

3. ADVERTISING

The App may show ads provided by third-party advertising networks such as
Google AdMob. These networks may use the Advertising ID and other device
signals to serve and measure ads. You can reset or limit your Advertising ID at
any time in your device settings (Settings > Google > Ads on Android). For more
information about how Google uses data, see:
https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

4. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY

The App is suitable for general audiences. We do not knowingly collect personal
information from children under the age of 13 (or the age required by your
country). Where the App is directed to children or used by children, we instruct
our advertising partners to serve only non-personalized, age-appropriate ads. If
you believe a child has provided personal information, please contact us and we
will take appropriate steps to address it.

5. DATA SHARING

We do not sell your personal information. Information collected automatically by
our third-party partners is processed by those partners as described in their
own privacy policies. We may disclose information if required to do so by law or
to protect our rights.

6. DATA SECURITY

We take reasonable measures to protect information. However, no method of
electronic storage or transmission is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee
absolute security.

7. DATA RETENTION AND DELETION

Game data is stored only on your device. You can delete all of it at any time by
clearing the App's data in your device settings or by uninstalling the App. Data
collected by third-party advertising or analytics partners is retained according
to their respective policies.

8. YOUR RIGHTS

Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete
personal information, or to object to certain processing. To exercise these
rights, contact us using the details below. You can also control ad
personalization through your device's Advertising ID settings.

9. INTERNATIONAL USERS

The App may be used worldwide. By using the App, you understand that information
collected by our third-party partners may be processed in countries other than
your own.

10. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted at
this page with a new "Last updated" date. Your continued use of the App after
changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.

